%% Bunny OS Phase 1 — Diagram 8 (file 13): Failure and Recovery
%% Interruption during a file-changing task, then recovery after restart.
%% The hard case is the window between "side effect happened" and
%% "state recorded" — §25.4 addresses it and this diagram shows where it sits.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SH as Bunny Shell
    participant BR as Bunny Broker
    participant PE as Plan Engine
    participant POL as Policy Evaluator
    participant EC as Execution Controller
    participant GL as Grant Ledger
    participant URS as Update and Recovery Service
    participant SM as Sandbox Manager
    participant SBX as Sandbox
    participant AUD as Audit Service
    participant J as Durable Event Journal

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over PE,AUD: BEFORE THE CRASH
    PE->>EC: execute exact ActionSpec op-1 — rewrite 40 files
    EC->>URS: create recovery point
    URS->>URS: workspace snapshot + plan version pin
    URS->>J: append owner-authorized RecoveryPoint event + outbox
    J-->>URS: durable receipt
    EC->>SM: prepare repository-modification profile<br/>with no usable capability
    SM->>SBX: create
    EC->>GL: prepare authorization reservation mutation
    GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
    EC->>AUD: prepare AuditStart mutation
    AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
    EC->>J: admitEffect batch<br/>(reservation + ExecutionStarted + AuditStart)
    J-->>EC: all owner events + outbox fsynced
    Note over EC,J: only now may the op-1 capability exist
    EC->>SBX: materialize capability and begin op-1
    SBX-->>EC: 18 of 40 files written
    end

    rect rgb(58, 34, 34)
    Note over PE,AUD: CRASH — power loss mid-step
    SBX--xEC: process dies
    end

    rect rgb(40, 48, 58)
    Note over U,AUD: RESTART
    EC->>J: read ExecutionAttempt owner stream
    J-->>EC: op-1 admitted with no terminal batch
    EC->>SM: reconcile — is the sandbox context orphaned?
    SM-->>EC: context gone
    EC->>URS: compare recovery point, base hashes and workspace
    URS-->>EC: possible effect — 18 exact file diffs observed
    EC->>GL: prepare Indeterminate reservation terminal
    GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
    EC->>AUD: prepare Indeterminate AuditTerminal
    AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
    EC->>J: finalizeEffect recovery batch<br/>(Grant + Execution + Audit = Indeterminate)
    J-->>EC: atomic terminal receipt

    EC->>PE: step 3 outcome = Indeterminate<br/>with reconciliation evidence
    PE->>SH: resume view from current plan version

    SH->>U: "Step 3 has an indeterminate outcome.<br/>18 of 40 intended file changes are visible.<br/>Restore from the recovery point, review the diff,<br/>or construct a new action for remaining work?"

    Note over SH,U: the state is NOT silently continued —<br/>resumption re-validates first and states<br/>its assumptions (Phase 0 §9)

    alt restore
        U->>SH: construct and review an exact restore
        SH->>BR: authenticated construction request, not approval
        BR->>PE: construct compensation ActionSpec op-2<br/>with canonical WorkspaceApplyManifest
        PE-->>BR: exact manifest, base generation,<br/>recovery point and ActionSpec hash
        BR->>GL: createRequest(op-2 effect + plan hashes<br/>and rendered restore digest)
        GL-->>BR: new request id + expected version + digest
        BR->>SH: display overwritten paths, exact diff and blast radius
        U->>SH: approve exact restore once
        SH->>BR: authenticated request-bound decision
        BR->>GL: recordDecision(request id,<br/>expected version, displayed digest)
        GL->>J: append decision + GrantIssued + outbox
        J-->>AUD: committed authorization event
        BR->>EC: execute compensation ActionSpec op-2
        EC->>URS: create pre-restore recovery point
        URS->>J: append RecoveryPoint event + outbox
        J-->>URS: durable receipt
        EC->>URS: prepareBaseApply(manifest)<br/>with no usable authority
        EC->>POL: evaluateForAdmission(op-2,<br/>current base, context and epochs)
        POL-->>EC: fresh user-grant-required AdmissionEvaluation
        EC->>GL: prepare op-2 reservation mutation
        GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>AUD: prepare op-2 AuditStart mutation
        AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>J: admitEffect op-2 batch<br/>(Grant + ExecutionStarted + AuditStart)
        J-->>EC: fsynced admission receipt
        EC->>URS: applyApprovedDiff(receipt, exact manifest)
        URS->>URS: validate epochs, recovery point,<br/>base CAS, paths, types and preimages
        URS-->>EC: observed postimage digests
        EC->>EC: verify every manifest entry
        EC->>GL: prepare op-2 reservation terminal
        GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>AUD: prepare op-2 AuditTerminal
        AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>J: finalizeEffect op-2 batch<br/>(Grant + Execution + Audit terminal)
        J-->>EC: atomic terminal receipt
    else construct remaining-work action
        U->>SH: propose remaining work
        SH->>BR: authenticated revision request
        BR->>PE: re-validate current context and revise plan
        PE-->>BR: new exact ActionSpec op-2 for remaining targets
        BR->>GL: createRequest(op-2 effect + plan hashes)
        GL-->>BR: new request id + expected version + digest
        BR->>SH: display new request — no implicit continuation
    end
    end

    Note over EC,J: RESIDUAL RISK, stated honestly (§26):<br/>an admitted attempt with no terminal batch means<br/>the effect may have happened. Reconciliation is read-only.<br/>Continuation always needs a new ActionSpec, operation id<br/>and authorization. Non-idempotent effects never auto-retry.
